@startuml test-pyramid
title Test pyramid — what gates what (test-specs/README.md, ADR-0007)
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

package "Tier 1 — ut: pure hostile parsing (no I/O)" #DDF0DD {
  component "tst/ut: corpus + semantics + compact + voices · 63 tests\nfindings F4, F5, F6 pinned green · MQTC binary contract" as L1
}
package "Tier 2 — ct: component vs mocks (local TCP + temp dirs)" #DDF0DD {
  component "tst/ct: hostile_http + disk_cache + disk · 26 tests\nfindings F1, F2 pinned green · F3 residual" as L2
}
package "Tier 3 — fuzz: deterministic mutation (temp dirs)" #DDF0DD {
  component "tst/fuzz: search model · URL builder · snapshot layer · MQTC · 6 tests\nfinding F10 pinned green" as L3
}
package "Hostile-in-the-Loop (not in cargo test)" #FFF6DD {
  component "e2e world tour — 100+ live mosques\nignore-annotated · just live" as H1
  component "libFuzzer campaign — parse_page, conf_pipeline\njust fuzz" as H2
  component "findings ledger audit — all fixed,\nregression tests run in cargo test" as H3
}

component "just verify:\nfmt → clippy -D warnings → check → targets-mcu → test → doc → smoke" as GATE #FFE9C8

GATE --> L1
GATE --> L2
GATE --> L3
component "release / weekly" as REL
REL --> H1
REL --> H2
REL --> H3
component "findings ledger\n(test-specs/README.md)" as LEDGER
H3 --> LEDGER

note as N1
  Tier guarantees nobody above re-checks:
  · ut — hostile bytes/JSON cannot panic, hang, or lie through the
    parse/calendar/MQTC path
  · ct — the client survives a lying server; the snapshot layer honors
    its store/fallback contract
  · fuzz — mutation space beyond the corpus is safe, reproducibly, in CI
  · HIL — the real site's real data parses everywhere

  Rule of thumb: pure input→behavior ⇒ ut; socket/file but not the real
  site ⇒ ct; new surface over attacker-shaped data ⇒ seed fuzz + corpus;
  real-site claim ⇒ e2e fixture; not-yet-true security behavior ⇒
  ignore-annotated finding test (ADR-0006).
end note
@enduml
